silica_rt_supervisor_which_children_acb:
# rdi = the held supervisor ACB -> rdi = the List of child-info records { id, agent_type, child, restart }
# (one 40-byte inline record per live row in a 56-byte chunk {record, pad, next}, with a 24-byte handle
# {length, first chunk, cursor 0} per chunk, as the compiled list prims read an inline-record list), or 0
# when no row is live. Chunk 15 stage 4e (design §9.1): the live rows are counted first, 120 bytes per row
# are reserved below rsp in this frame as a destination area (its pair at [rbp - 96]), the list is built
# there back to front through silica_rt_dest_take, and the routine leaves through rbp with rsp at the
# area's bottom, so silica_rt_sup_ref_call passes the lowered rsp on and the emitted call site adopts
# the list into the caller's frame (prims_actors@runtime_call_asm).
# [rbp - 8] ACB (x19), [rbp - 16] row (x20), [rbp - 24] list so far (x21), [rbp - 32] child (x22),
# [rbp - 40] info record (x23), [rbp - 48] id, then chunk (x24), [rbp - 56] agent (x25), [rbp - 64] restart (x26),
# [rbp - 72] new list handle (x27), [rbp - 96] / [rbp - 88] the destination pair.
