# with nothing committed (_silica_rt_actor_stack_reserve stores 0 at #288), and the first call here is
# the spawn's install, before the child has run a single instruction; a release of an EMPTY area
# (_silica_rt_stack_release_to) also leaves the header decommitted. When the committed run [top - #288,
# top) does not reach top - 1040, commit the top chunk through _silica_rt_stack_grow_to: a fresh commit
# (first mprotect, or the anonymous MAP_FIXED remap of a release) reads as zero, so the 129 heads are
# empty without initialisation (§2.3); the chunk is the same first chunk a fault would commit (#304),
# so the release algorithms' chunk sequence is unchanged. Answer 1 (a lowered reservation of one
# page: the lowest page is never committed) or 2 (the host refused) is a state the reservation cannot
# hold, 0 to the caller (decision 39). Answer 3 cannot occur here: it means the run already reaches
