# new state makes the behaviour unproven, so every retire() logged in a proven dispatch is of an old
# node whose updated version was discarded, and the new state may still hold it. The log is drained
# only when the behaviour epilogue's buffer retire wrote it (#560 = 2: it emptied the log first and
# then logged the old buffers the new state does not keep, prims_actors@bmv_state_buffer_retire_asm);
